WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.957
Schema inference is convenient for exploration.

00:00:02.957 --> 00:00:05.942
Spark can look at data and guess types.

00:00:05.942 --> 00:00:13.912
But inferred types can be wrong, especially for identifiers, dates, mixed values, or sparse columns.

00:00:13.912 --> 00:00:22.082
For production workflows and important assignments, an explicit schema is often safer because it documents the

00:00:22.082 --> 00:00:22.582
expected structure.

00:00:22.582 --> 00:00:29.297
Schema inference is convenient for exploration, but production pipelines benefit from explicit schemas.

00:00:29.297 --> 00:00:36.982
A single malformed file or unexpected type can change inference or force expensive extra scans.

00:00:36.982 --> 00:00:42.766
Defining types up front also documents expectations and catches defects earlier.
